# AssistantOrb - the assistant, as a living sphere of light with eyes: light flows inside it (a WebGL shader), it
# breathes, blinks, glances around and follows the pointer over the area around it, and smiles when it has done
# something. Without WebGL it is the same sphere as a gradient; with reduced motion it stays still, eyes open.
#   AssistantOrb(size: "240")
# Its mood is set from outside with an event on its element: el.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("orb:mood",
# { detail: { happy: 1, energy: 1, look: { x: -1, y: -.5 }, bump: true } })) - happy 0..1 (the smile), energy 0..1
# (the light speeds up and turns mint), look -1..1 (null = its own glances), bump (a little jump). AssistantPlay
# drives it that way.
# look: "" | left | right - where its eyes rest when idle (toward the form beside it, say); it still glances around
# that point, blinks, and follows the pointer.
# size: the sphere's box in px (the sphere and its halo fill it). The pointer area is the closest element with
# data-area="orb", else its parent.
# shadcn-for-muten · Custom · kit.css (.cx-orb) · host JS assistant-orb.js.
part AssistantOrb(size: text = "240", look: text = "") { Custom AssistantOrb inputs(size: $size, look: $look) class("cx-orb") }
